      "hints": [
        "In $\\triangle DBC$, $BD = 20\\sin\\theta$.",
        "In $\\triangle ABD$, $\\angle ABD = \\theta \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\frac{9}{BD} \\implies BD = \\frac{9}{\\tan\\theta}$.",
        "Equate: $20\\sin\\theta = \\frac{9\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} \\implies 20\\sin^2\\theta = 9\\cos\\theta$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express $BD$ using the right-angled triangle $DBC$ (hypotenuse $BC = 20$ cm):\n$$\\sin\\theta = \\frac{BD}{20} \\implies BD = 20\\sin\\theta$$",
        "Express $BD$ using the right-angled triangle $ABD$ (where $\\angle ABD = 90^\\circ - (90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\theta$ and $AD = 9$ cm):\n$$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{AD}{BD} = \\frac{9}{BD} \\implies BD = \\frac{9}{\\tan\\theta} = \\frac{9\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}$$",
        "Equate both expressions for $BD$ and simplify:\n$$20\\sin\\theta = \\frac{9\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} \\implies 20\\sin^2\\theta = 9\\cos\\theta$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
